# Feature: Workflow & process engine

Every design moves through configurable Main Processes and Sub-processes.
**Runtime behavior is driven by `StageCapabilities` on `DesignSubProcessMaster`
(JSON) via `resolveStageBehavior` - codes are stable IDs only, never behavior switches.**

## Master data
- `DesignProcessMaster`: ProcessId, Code, Name, Sequence, Active.
- `DesignSubProcessMaster`: SubProcessId, ProcessId, Code, Name, Sequence,
  DefaultRole, IsApproval, IsCorrectionAllowed, IsFileRequired, **Capabilities (JSON)**, Active.
- `WorkflowPattern` / `WorkflowPatternTask`: reusable templates; optional
  `capabilitiesOverride` per step for rare pattern-specific tweaks.

## Capabilities (source of truth)
See `src/lib/workflow/stage-capabilities.ts` and `resolveStageBehavior`.
Key flags: `isApproval`, `requiresFile`, `forcesChecking`, `machineOutput`,
`sampleDecisionOutcomes`, `costingEntry`, `completeNotChecking`,
`approvalSurface` / `approvalActions`, `workPrecursor`,
`unlockAfterDesignApproved`, `autoAdvanceOnCreate`, `onComplete` hooks.

## Transition data gates
Cross-stage requirements (e.g. cost entries before approve-for-production) live in
`src/lib/workflow/transition-policies.ts` - presence-driven from capabilities on
instantiated tasks. Do not hardcode module checks in approval/UI callers.

## Authoring a custom workflow
1. Create sub-processes in Admin → Masters with capabilities (not only isApproval/file).
2. Compose a Workflow Pattern from those steps (owner role + minutes + deps).
3. Validation blocks approvals without surface/owner/precursor when required.
4. Post-approval ladder stages are those with `unlockAfterDesignApproved`
   (textile PROD_* remain the seeded default).
5. No new `if (code === "…")` should be required in app logic for a new stage.

## Rule
Do not hardcode employee names in workflow patterns. Store `RoleId`;
resolve to an eligible employee only at task-generation time.

## API
- `GET /api/masters/processes` - process/sub-process master (includes capabilities).
- `GET /api/workflow-patterns` - workflow pattern definitions.
